filiated Faculty\nResearchers and Postdocs\nGraduate Students\nStaff\nUndergraduate\nApply Now\nCareers in Geosciences\nPrograms\nGeology Major\nEarth and Space Sciences Major\nEarth Science Education\nGraduate\nApplicant FAQs\nGraduate Programs Handbook\nPrograms\nPhD in Geosciences\nMasters Degrees\nApply Now\nPhD. Application Fee Waivers\nResearch\nDepartment Research Areas\nDepartment Labs\nDavid E. King Field Work Award\nDEI\nOutreach\nGeology Open Nights\nGraduates for Education and Outreach (GEO)\nGiving\nTBI Field Camp\nDepartment of Geosciences\nGraduate\nApply Now\nPh.D.Application Fee Waivers\nPhD Application Fee Waivers\nApplication fee waivers are available for a limited number of Geosciences Ph.D. applicants\n(domestic and international).\nPlease submit requests here. Waivers will be accepted through December 15, 2026.\nNote: We cannot waive fees for applications that have already been submitted.\nTo be considered for the fee waiver you should have, or will have by the end of Spring\n2027, the equivalent of a 4 year undergraduate degree and/or a Masters degree in earth\nsciences, space sciences, biology, chemistry, physics, mathematics, or engineering.\nYou should have the equivalent of a U.S. GPA of at least 3.25. In addition to academic\nperformance, we will also consider the research interests of the student and how well\nthey match our program. Note that being successful in the pre-application for the\nfee waiver is in no way a guarantee of admission. If your fee waiver request is declined,\nyou will be required to pay the fee in order for your application to be considered\nfor admission.\nFooter\nDepartment of Geosciences\n255 Earth and Space Science Building | Stony Brook, NY 11794-2100\nPHONE: (631) 632-8200\nPrivacy Policy\nReporting Discrimination\nSexual Misconduct\nAccessibility Barrier\n\u00a9 2026 Stony Brook University\n\u00a9", "links": [["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/"], ["Department of Geosciences", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/geosci